m/users/stuartcarnie","html_url":"https://github.com/stuartcarnie","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/stuartcarnie/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-25T21:21:28Z","updated_at":"2024-11-25T21:21:28Z","body":"> On my m2 MBA I setup a simple 30s benchmark scene moving a camera around bistro for various scaling factors and saw a roughly 19% improvement going from fsr2 to MetalFX temporal.\r\n\r\nHow did you set up the 30s benchmark? Presumably it follows the same path every time, so it is repeatable?","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2499061901/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2499096470","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99603#issuecomment-2499096470","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99603","id":2499096470,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6U9S-W","user":{"login":"a-johnston","id":9058941,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjkwNTg5NDE=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/9058941?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston","html_url":"https://github.com/a-johnston","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/a-johnston/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-11-25T21:43:20Z","updated_at":"2024-11-25T21:43:20Z","body":"> How did you set up the 30s benchmark? Presumably it follows the same path every time, so it is repeatable?\r\n\r\nYeah super simple, just a camera on a set position/rotation path to get a somewhat representative sample of the bistro scene with a process step that moves the camera and counts frames until 30s of benchmark have passed at which point it reports the average for that period and quits. Definitely a lot of possible improvements to make but I just wanted a rough idea of the performance difference. If it would be helpful I can make some changes to it and share it here but it took maybe a minute or two to set up.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2499096470/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":1,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2510135022","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/99603#issuecomment-2510135022","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/99603","id":2510135022,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6VnZ7u","us